From b70d9ac8e3d13a7433177b23ba54490322ebe3c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:43:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/47] lexi: explain why the nixbld group id is set

The comment called the setting temporary, but lexi cannot drop it: its
nixbld group has GID 350, nix-darwin defaults to 30000 at state version
4, and the activation check aborts when the two differ.  Say so, so that
the setting is not removed by mistake.
---
 machines/darwin/lexi.nix | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/machines/darwin/lexi.nix b/machines/darwin/lexi.nix
index 872bbaf..f70c18c 100644
--- a/machines/darwin/lexi.nix
+++ b/machines/darwin/lexi.nix
@@ -1,6 +1,11 @@
 { ... }:
 {
-  ids.gids.nixbld = 350; # temp
+  /*
+    The Nix installer of this machine created the nixbld group with GID
+    350, while nix-darwin expects 30000 at state version 4 and refuses
+    to activate when they differ.
+  */
+  ids.gids.nixbld = 350;
 
   imports = [
     ./state-version.nix
-- 
2.56.1

